---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import OrderReview from '../components/OrderReview.astro';
import DemoCTA from '../components/DemoCTA.astro';
const details = [
  ['Browse', 'Start with a digital menu.', 'Customers explore products on the kiosk touchscreen and browse the available categories before making a choice.'],
  ['Select', 'Add what looks good.', 'Customers choose food and beverages and add products to their cart. Their selection comes together in one place.'],
  ['Adjust', 'Make the selection right.', 'Customers adjust quantities and manage the items in the cart before moving to the review step.'],
  ['Review', 'See the order and the total.', 'The review brings together the chosen products, quantities, and calculated total, giving customers a chance to check their order.'],
  ['Confirm', 'Take the next step with clarity.', 'Customers proceed to order confirmation on the kiosk. Payment processing, printer output, POS connections, and kitchen order handling remain planned integrations.'],
];
---
<Layout title="How EZ Kyosk Self-Ordering Works" description="Browse, select, adjust, review and confirm. Learn how customers use the EZ Kyosk touchscreen ordering experience and which integrations are planned.">
  <section class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS / FROM MENU TO CONFIRMATION</div><h1>Five simple steps.<br /><em>One simple screen.</em></h1><p>Browse → Select → Adjust → Review → Confirm. A clear path through the self-ordering experience, with room to check each choice.</p></section>
  <div class="page-body">
    <div class="feature-section" style="margin-bottom:55px"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR MENU. THEIR ORDER.</div><h2>Customers stay<br />in control of their selection.</h2><p style="margin-top:24px">The kiosk is the place to browse, build a cart, and review the total. Your team can focus on food preparation and customer service.</p><p>This page explains the product journey. This marketing website does not accept food orders.</p></div><OrderReview /></div>
    {details.map(([label, title, body], i) => <section class="step-detail"><span>0{i + 1}</span><div><div class="eyebrow">{label}</div><h2>{title}</h2></div><p>{body}</p></section>)}
    <div class="notice">Order confirmation is part of the described product journey. It does not mean that a payment has been collected or an order has reached a printer, kitchen, or POS.</div>
  </div>
  <DemoCTA />
</Layout>
